You are absolutely right. Because we set paginationMode="server", the React frontend only has 10 rows in its memory at any given time. MUI's default client-side filter can only search through those 10 rows, which completely breaks the search for older batches.
To fix this, we need to switch the DataGrid to filterMode="server" and pass the search text all the way back to your Oracle database.
Here are the exact changes needed on both the Frontend and the Backend.
### Part 1: Frontend Changes (VoucherPostingStatus.jsx)
**1. Add the Filter State**
At the top of your component, right near your paginationModel state, add a new state to track what the user is typing into the filter box.
```javascript
  const [paginationModel, setPaginationModel] = useState({ page: 0, pageSize: 10 });
  const [totalRowCount, setTotalRowCount] = useState(0);
  
  // --- ADD THIS NEW STATE ---
  const [filterModel, setFilterModel] = useState({ items: [] });

```
**2. Update fetchMyBatches to send the filters**
Inside your fetchMyBatches function, we need to extract the search text from the filterModel and append it to the API URL.
```javascript
